---
title: "claimTokenAllocation (LegionFixedPriceSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_paused: check contract not paused
    q_check_paused --> q_check_supplied: not paused
    q_check_paused --> q_revert: revert Paused
    q_check_supplied --> q_check_settled: tokens have been supplied
    q_check_supplied --> q_revert: revert TokensNotSupplied
    q_check_settled --> q_verify_merkle: position.hasSettled == false
    q_check_settled --> q_revert: revert AlreadyClaimed
    q_verify_merkle --> q_calc_allocation: Merkle proof valid for (investor, allocation)
    q_verify_merkle --> q_revert: revert InvalidMerkleProof
    q_calc_allocation --> q_check_vesting: calculate token allocation from proof
    q_check_vesting --> q_deploy_vesting: vesting schedule required
    q_check_vesting --> q_direct_transfer: immediate distribution
    q_deploy_vesting --> q_transfer_to_vesting: deploy vesting contract via clone pattern
    q_transfer_to_vesting --> q_mark_settled: transfer tokens to vesting contract
    q_direct_transfer --> q_mark_settled: transfer tokens to investor
    q_mark_settled --> [*]: position.hasSettled = true, emit TokensClaimed
    q_revert --> [*]: revert with error

    note right of q_verify_merkle
        INV-001: Merkle proof must match published claimMerkleRoot
        INV-002: each investor can claim exactly once (hasSettled flag)
    end note

    note right of q_deploy_vesting
        INV-003: vesting contract deployed via EIP-1167 minimal proxy clone
        INV-004: vesting address stored in position for future releaseVestedTokens calls
    end note
